# * register --chart and svg output

<
2024-01-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-01-05
    expenses:food      30
    assets:bank

2024-02-01
    assets:bank       100
    revenues:salary

2024-02-10
    expenses:rent      80
    liabilities:card

# ** 1. Without a report interval, the chart data is the running total after each posting, as a line by date; with postings to several accounts, also each account's own running total.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","expenses:food","item","line","2024-01-05","30"
"","expenses:food","item","line","2024-02-10","30"
"","expenses:rent","item","line","2024-01-05","0"
"","expenses:rent","item","line","2024-02-10","80"
"","Total","total","line","2024-01-05","30"
"","Total","total","line","2024-02-10","110"

# ** 2. With postings to one account, it is just the running total.
$ hledger -f - reg rent --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","Total","item","line","2024-02-10","80"

# ** 3. With a report interval, it is each account's amount in each period, as stacked bars, with the period total as a marker.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses -M --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","expenses:food","item","bar","Jan","30"
"","expenses:food","item","bar","Feb","0"
"","expenses:rent","item","bar","Jan","0"
"","expenses:rent","item","bar","Feb","80"
"","Total","total","marker","Jan","30"
"","Total","total","marker","Feb","80"

# ** 4. A text chart has a row per posting, with the accounts' running totals stacked, and the overall running total as the value.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses --chart -w 40
█ expenses:food  ▓ expenses:rent

2024-01-05   30  ██████▎
2024-02-10  110  ██████▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓▓

# ** 5. With -H, each account's running total starts from its balance before the report period, so they add up to the overall (historical) running total.
$ hledger -f - reg expenses -b 2024-02 -H --chart -O csv
"commodity","series","role","mark","x","value"
"","expenses:food","item","line","2024-02-10","30"
"","expenses:rent","item","line","2024-02-10","80"
"","Total","total","line","2024-02-10","110"
